{"qid":"Q1025803","names":["Cai"],"title":"Cai","endonym":null,"capsule":"Cai was a Zhou dynasty vassal state founded when King Wu of Zhou granted the title to his younger brother Shu Du after the defeat of the Shang dynasty around 1046 BCE, centred near present-day Shangcai in Henan province with later capitals further east in the Huai River basin. During the Spring and Autumn period it was a recognised but weak principality buffeted by larger powers, particularly Chu to the south, which forced Cai to relocate its capital multiple times under sustained military pressure. Cai was finally destroyed by Chu around 447 BCE, ending approximately six centuries of nominal Zhou vassalage.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Cai's general location in Henan and the Huai basin is well-attested in the Zuozhuan and other classical Chinese records; the state's shifting capitals make precise territorial mapping uncertain for different sub-periods.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Cai (state)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cai_(state)"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Spring and Autumn period","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spring_and_Autumn_period"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Zhou dynasty","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zhou_dynasty"}],"britannica":null,"cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Cai (state)","rulers":[{"qid":null,"name":"Marquis Yi of Cai","nativeName":"蔡夷侯","roman":"Cài Yí Hóu","start":-837,"end":-762,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Marquis Xi of Cai","nativeName":"蔡釐侯","roman":"Cài Xí Hóu","start":-761,"end":-714,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{